        "text": "Prior/update/interval: persistence prior = 13.4%. PolicyEngine's direct model input gives -0.1966pp, rounded to a -0.2pp directional inside-view update; because the live 2027 economy run was unfinished, it is not treated as a completed 2027 estimate. No separate momentum or macro update is supported, so point = 13.4 - 0.2 = 13.2%. From fetched successive changes [-2.9, -4.5, 7.2, 1.3, -0.3], sample sigma = 4.5319pp. The nominal 80% half-width is 1.28*sigma = 1.28 \u00d7 4.5319 = 5.8008pp. Widen by 1.10 for the announced revised-methodology transition, the unfinished live 2027 PolicyEngine run, and the limitation of calibrating volatility from only five annual changes: 5.8008 \u00d7 1.10 = 6.3809pp. Thus 13.2 \u00b1 6.3809 = [6.8191, 19.5809], published as [6.8, 19.6]. Four of the five observed annual moves\u201480%\u2014fit within \u00b16.3809pp."
