      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Mechanism and counter-consideration: the condition reaches very-low-earning families by starting the ACTC phase-in near the first dollar, but the unchanged 15% rate limits the mechanical gain to roughly $375 and nonfiling can prevent take-up. The modeled -0.2pp effect is therefore applied once, not double-counted with the 2021 expanded-CTC observation. Upside risk would land above the interval if the revised SPM methodology sharply raises measured child poverty while a recession substantially reduces low-income earnings. Downside risk would land below the interval if unexpectedly strong earnings combine with much broader refundable-credit legislation or unusually complete filing take-up."
